<h2>Compare Fractions with the Same Denominator</h2>
<p>Original source warm-up Two More Strips is an open visual notice-and-wonder with a partly covered strip, not a fixed numeric question.</p>
<h3>All six original required fraction comparisons</h3><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>First source fraction</th><th>Relation</th><th>Second source fraction</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>1/2</th><td>&lt;</td><td>3/2</td></tr>
<tr><th>3/8</th><td>&gt;</td><td>2/8</td></tr>
<tr><th>1/6</th><td>&lt;</td><td>4/6</td></tr>
<tr><th>4/4</th><td>&lt;</td><td>5/4</td></tr>
<tr><th>2/3</th><td>&gt;</td><td>1/3</td></tr>
<tr><th>4/8</th><td>&lt;</td><td>6/8</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>OPTIONAL: Find a missing numerator</h3><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Original inequality</th><th>Valid condition</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>1/2 &lt; n/2</td><td>n&gt;1</td></tr>
<tr><td>6/4 &gt; n/4</td><td>n&lt;6</td></tr>
<tr><td>4/3 &lt; n/3</td><td>n&gt;4</td></tr>
<tr><td>5/8 &gt; n/8</td><td>n&lt;5</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Spin to Win: Same Denominator</h3><p>Use two different colors, ten rounds and source denominator choices <strong>2,3,4,6,8</strong>. Highest initial spinner selects Player1, who chooses a denominator for round one. Each player spins numerator, marks the fraction on the same number line, and the player with the larger fraction selects the next denominator. Student rolls and decisions are variable; teacher reviews actual ten-round record.</p>
<p>The publisher's partly obscured photograph/spinner original and gated Cool-down were not copied. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-5/lesson-15/lesson.html">Original 2021 teacher source</a>.</p></section>